duction","label":"Visualisation de la traduction","html_id":"visualisation-de-la-traduction","implicit":true,"key":"G0rO4VbXXl"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":92,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Notre prochain objectif est de tracer la traduction d’une propriété et de voir si\nnous pouvons observer n’importe quel mode de traduction. Veuillez copier le code ci-dessous et\ncréer de nouvelles cellules pour les tests avec des propriétés différentes et tracer la\nrésultats. Dans ce graphique, nous traçons le temps sur l’axe des x et la traduction\ntapez sur l’axe des y.","position":{"start":{"line":88,"column":1},"end":{"line":88,"column":1}},"key":"J5TPLv4oVP"}],"key":"IBFUI6YHjg"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"import matplotlib \nimport  matplotlib.pyplot as plot \nfrom  dateutil import parser \nimport  numpy as np  \nptranslation  = dataframe.loc[(dataframe[\"property\"]==\"P856\")]  \nx  = [] \ny  = [] \nz  = [] \nfor  i in range(0, len(ptranslation['timestamp'])):\n    #parsing the date in string and converting it to datetime\n    try:\n        value = parser.parse(ptranslation['timestamp'].iloc[i])\n        x.append(value)\n    except Exception:\n        continue\n    y.append(ptranslation['type'].iloc[i])\n    z.append(ptranslation['language'].iloc[i])\n    \n#creating  a plot\nplot.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"]  = (25, 9) \ncolors  = matplotlib.cm.rainbow(np.linspace(0, 1, 3))\ntcolors  = {'label': colors[0],\n      'description':colors[1],\n      'alias':colors[2]\n     }\ncs  = [tcolors[i] for i in y]  \nfig,  ax = plot.subplots() \nax.scatter(x, y, s=30, color=cs)  \n\nplot.xlabel(\"Time\") \nplot.ylabel(\"Translation type\")  \n\n#annotating  the points \nfor i, txt in enumerate(z):\n   ax.annotate(txt, (x[i], y[i]))\n\nfig.show()             ","position":{"start":{"line":94,"column":1},"end":{"line":132,"column":1}},"key":"dbTFn21cQu"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":135,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Maintenant, nous traçons un autre graphique, cette fois-ci, la langue sur l’axe des y et le temps\nsur l’axe des x.","position":{"start":{"line":134,"column":1},"end":{"line":134,"column":1}},"key":"wCITV8Rhfh"}],"key":"NSgG6vNchB"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"import matplotlib \nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plot \nfrom dateutil import parser \nimport numpy as np  \n\nptranslation = dataframe.loc[(dataframe[\"property\"]==\"P279\")]  \nx = [] \ny = [] \nz = [] \n\nfor i in range(0, len(ptranslation['timestamp'])):\n    try:\n      #parsing the date in string and converting it to datetime\n      value = parser.parse(ptranslation['timestamp'].iloc[i])\n      x.append(value)\n    except Exception:\n      continue\n    y.append(ptranslation['type'].iloc[i])\n    z.append(ptranslation['language'].iloc[i])  \n\n#creating a plot \ncolors = matplotlib.cm.rainbow(np.linspace(0, 1, 3)) \ntcolors = {'label': colors[0],\n               'description':colors[1],\n               'alias':colors[2]\n            } \n\ncs = [tcolors[i] for i in y]   \n\nplot.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"] = (25, 25)  \nfig, ax = plot.subplots() \nax.scatter(x, z, s=50, color=cs)   \n\nplot.xlabel(\"Time\") \nplot.ylabel(\"Language\")  \n\n# saving the plot in a file \nplot.savefig('translation.png') \nfig.show()             ","position":{"start":{"line":137,"column":1},"end":{"line":177,"column":1}},"key":"RdER4MCShz"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":179,"column":1},"end":{"line":183,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Voici trois graphiques concernant les propriétés : P31, P279 et P856\nrespectivement. Quelles sont vos observations sur les valeurs sur l’axe des y ?\nVeuillez les noter en tant que commentaires sur le notebook. Vous pouvez également constater que certains\ntraductions peuvent même être effectuées en une seule fois. Veuillez vérifier une colonne de\nlignes rouges dans le premier graphique (P31).","position":{"start":{"line":179,"column":1},"end":{"line":179,"column":1}},"key":"mfPjsWR0OJ"}],"key":"GGtL4KwLkE"},{"type":"image","url":"/IA-DeepLearning/build/p31-1bf1a0ade430352b5007009f234c7f81.png","alt":"Translation plot of property P31","position":{"start":{"line":185,"column":1},"end":{"line":185,"column":1}},"key":"bfnMpb2bBq","urlSource":"../../en/Project/p31.png"},{"type":"image","url":"/IA-DeepLearning/build/p279-b0095e89e937a9800312b6d715612fd7.png","alt":"Translation plot of property P279","position":{"start":{"line":187,"column":1},"end":{"line":187,"column":1}},"key":"jYIn59BaL5","urlSource":"../../en/Project/p279.png"},{"type":"image","url":"/IA-DeepLearning/build/p856-73665a7e95927c1daf45093fe8efdc88.png","alt":"Translation plot of property P856","position":{"start":{"line":189,"column":1},"end":{"line":189,"column":1}},"key":"UuY0nBQD3A","urlSource":"../../en/Project/p856.png"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":191,"column":1},"end":{"line":193,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Dans le code donné ci-dessous, nous sélectionnons quelques langues et voyons l’ordre de\ntraduction. Copiez le code ci-dessous et tracez les graphiques pour les différents\npropriétés. Veuillez noter vos observations.","position":{"start":{"line":191,"column":1},"end":{"line":191,"column":1}},"key":"PUSjVjZR8c"}],"key":"TBFamIPPdF"},{"type":"code","lang":"","value":"import matplotlib \nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plot \nfrom dateutil import parser \nimport numpy as np  \n\n#list of languages under consideration \nlanglist  = [\"fr\", \"es\", \"en\", \"de\", \"it\", \"pt\", \"ja\"] \nptranslation  = dataframe.loc[(dataframe[\"property\"]==\"P18\") & (dataframe[\"language\"].isin (langlist))] \nprint(ptranslation)  \n\nx= [] \ny= [] \nz= [] \n\nfor i in range(0, len(ptranslation['timestamp'])):\n    try:\n        #parsing the date in string and converting it to datetime\n        value = parser.parse(ptranslation['timestamp'].iloc[i])\n      x.append(value)\n    except Exception:\n      continue\n    y.append(ptranslation['type'].iloc[i])\n    z.append(ptranslation['language'].iloc[i])  \n\n#creating  a plot \ncolors  = matplotlib.cm.rainbow(np.linspace(0, 1, 3)) \ntcolors  = {'label': colors[0],\n               'description':colors[1],\n               'alias':colors[2]\n             } \n\ncs  = [tcolors[i] for i in y]   \nplot.rcParams[\"figure.figsize\"]  = (10, 5)  \nfig,  ax = plot.subplots() \nax.scatter(x,  z, s=50, color=cs)  \n\nplot.savefig('translation.png') \nfig.show()             ","position":{"start":{"line":195,"column":1},"end":{"line":234,"column":1}},"key":"S3rv8DwmFG"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"position":{"start":{"line":236,"column":1},"end":{"line":236,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Exercice 1.2","position":{"start":{"line":236,"column":1},"end":{"line":236,"column":1}},"key":"AoBTruOeAN"}],"identifier":"exercice-1-2","label":"Exercice 1.2","html_id":"exercice-1-2","implicit":true,"key":"J7x9WMRulE"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":240,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Nous avons utilisé des techniques de traçage pour détecter manuellement certains modes de\ntraduction. Nous utilisons maintenant d’autres algorithmes pour voir si des groupes de\nles langues sont toujours présentes ensemble","position":{"start":{"line":238,"column":1},"end":{"line":238,"column":1}},"key":"GHSwV6MCBX"}],"key":"h9ftFsnZ0Z"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":242,"column":1},"end":{"line":242,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Avant de continuer, nous devons installer la bibliothèque ","position":{"start":{"line":242,"column":1},"end":{"line":242,"column":1}},"key":"RAfnF71FB2"},{"type":"emphasis","position":{"start":{"line":242,"column":1},"end":{"line":242,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"mlxtend","position":{"start":{"line":242,"column":1},"end":{"line":242,"column":1}}